00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:05.480 align:start position:0%
Ubisoft has revealed its Battle Royale  FPS called hyper scape and I know what  you're thinking another Battle Royale  while it has many of the core tenants  you'd expect from the genre hyper scape  is trying some new things let's run down  everything that makes it unique revives  and responds when players die they're  not necessarily out of the game instead  they turn into invisible entities that  can still run around the map they just  can't do anything other than move what  this means is that dead teammates can  effectively be Scouts by spotting  enemies and watching their movements for  teammates who are still fighting this  makes death less of a punishment it  keeps you invested in the game and  further encourages communication even if  you die to respawn a teammate you need  to find a restore point which is created  where any opponent dies the dead player  needs to sit on it while an active  teammate revives them it can make for  aggressive play since you have to defeat  an opponent or track down a dead enemy  to bring back a teammate loot and gear  progression hyper scape doesn't feature  tears and colors for loot instead all  gear can be upgraded up to four times  throughout a match by finding duplicates  of them for example if you have an  assault rifle and loot another one it  then gets upgraded with a slight  magazine capacity increase and damage  boost in practice this incentivizes  looting even after you found your  favorite loadout special abilities are  called hacks which you'll also loot  during a match since the game's  characters don't function like heroes  you can custom fit which two abilities  you want when you find them on the map  it adds a bit of a strategic layer since  you could swap hacks throughout the  match and use the two you find most  effective in tandem hacks don't have  limited uses instead they run on  cooldown timers some of my favorites  were the teleport - temporary  invisibility a massive wall and a super  bouncy hamster ball like weapons you  have to loot duplicates of the same hack  to upgrade it which gets you shorter  cooldown timers  being crowned the winner you don't  necessarily have to be the last one  standing  to win in hyper scape when it gets down  to the last few squads a crown will  spawn on the map players can pick up the  crown which will then start a 45 second  countdown  if the crown holder can stay alive for  the entire 45 seconds their team wins  however the crown holders location will  be revealed to all the remaining players  when it's picked up leaving them open  for attack if your team thinks  tactically though you can set yourself  up to defend the crown holder or  effectively dodge death but if another  team picks it up  you better get after them fast how the  map shrinks players aren't forced in  from a deadly closing circle like most  battle Royales hyper escapes map is  designed to resemble a small city and  it's cut up and distinct chunks or  districts as the match progresses whole  sections get chopped off this is to  prevent situations where a circle would  awkwardly enclose players and buildings  and this prioritizes the intended map  design arena shooter vibes combat  encounters and hyper scape remind me of  Unreal Tournament or quake you have  double jumps jump pads no fall damage  and a fairly high time to kill it's fast  paced and the map is designed with  verticality in mind and your weapons  reflect the more arcade style feel you  have rocket launchers grenade launchers  chain guns shock rifles and more  conventional guns that function  similarly to how they do in arena  shooters rather than spotting players  from afar and then cutting them off with  a well-placed shot you'll initiate  fights with the intention of starting a  head-to-head shootout twitch audience  participation viewers on twitch streams  can participate in the game as well  hyper scape features a twitch extension  that lets a streamers viewers vote on in  match events these can range from  allowing triple jumps unlimited ammo  speed boosts and more for a short period  of time eventually viewers will also  gain in-game rewards and advance their  battle passes by participating streamers  will also be able to invite viewers to  squads easily through that twitch  extension however these features will be  implemented at a later date so those are  the notable features that can help hyper  scape stand out in the battle royale  space as of this video Ubisoft is  running a technical test currently only  on PC there are sure to be more details  on the game soon and when they come you  can find them here on GameSpot  you  [Music]
 

